[about]
Title=09 - Glossary
Intro=The words FileDir uses, in alphabetical order. I say the term; the reader says what it means.
Setup=Nothing is needed.
Homework=Pick three terms you did not know and find each one in FileDir.

[step]

Say=archive.
Key=
Hear=A zip or other packed file, opened like a folder with Enter. Shift plus Z makes one; Shift plus U unpacks one.

[step]

Say=extra info.
Key=
Hear=Everything known about the file or episode you are on, one field to a line. Alt plus X.

[step]

Say=filter.
Key=
Hear=The folder narrowed to the files matching a pattern, until cleared. Control plus F.

[step]

Say=folder.
Key=
Hear=A list of files and folders, said with its path and its count as you arrive. Enter goes in; Backspace comes up.

[step]

Say=Go To and Open.
Key=
Hear=Two ways to reach a folder: Go To, Control plus G, in this window; Open, Control plus O, in a new one.

[step]

Say=Homer Player.
Key=
Hear=The player shared by the Homer Tools: a queue of tracks, transport on Control plus the arrows, Scroll Lock to pause, and Alt plus Shift plus R to record.

[step]

Say=Initial Change.
Key=
Hear=The next name starting with a different letter. Shift plus I; Shift plus X for the next kind of file.

[step]

Say=jump.
Key=
Hear=Reaching a file by the line the list shows: type a few letters of its name. Control plus J.

[step]

Say=keywords.
Key=
Hear=A search across everything known about each file or episode: name, date, address, summary. Control plus K; F3 finds the next.

[step]

Say=play list.
Key=
Hear=Every media link a page holds, queued in the Homer Player. Control plus Shift plus L.

[step]

Say=Quick folder.
Key=
Hear=Your favorites: files, folders and web links. Shift plus Q adds one; Control plus Q opens the folder.

[step]

Say=recent folders.
Key=
Hear=Every folder opened this session, newest first. Alt plus R.

[step]

Say=rename.
Key=
Hear=A new name for the current file or folder. F2, or Shift plus R; Control plus R renames many with wildcards.

[step]

Say=status line.
Key=
Hear=The folder, the line, and how many files are tagged; the bottom of the window. Shift plus Z says it.

[step]

Say=tag.
Key=
Hear=A mark on a file so the next command acts on it and on every other tagged file. The semicolon tags and untags.

[step]

Say=transport.
Key=
Hear=Control with an arrow, in the player: sideways is time in the track, up and down is tracks, Page keys are chapters; Shift makes the step larger.

[step]

Say=What Content.
Key=
Hear=What is inside the current file: its kind, size and dates, read from the file itself. The question mark.

[step]

Say=word processor.
Key=
Hear=The program Control plus W opens the current file in, named in Configuration Options.

[step]

Say=Eighteen terms. The guide, F1, has each of them in context.
Key=
Hear=
